 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Pop the seat tube on one half off its bearings, carefully slide it back on, and then check that it' exactly level. The bike should rise a little but not too much. If it rises a lot, the seat tube isn't on the bearings properly. Say again? Your phone's voice recognition system must have cut out. Then raise your seat a bit more, and try pedaling again. Then your seat tube isn't on the bearings at all, and you need to take it apart and reassemble it. That's a bit trickier, so if you' not confident, get a shop to do it. You should still reach the ground with few inches to spare. If your seat is too high, you'll always be leaning forward.",
